	)
	(text "Data straight from the Pico's USB test points TP3 (D+) / TP2 (D-), behind the Pico's own 27R\nseries resistors (sheet 1). The Pico must be soldered FLAT on the board (castellated edge or\nthrough-hole pins, no header) so TP1-TP3 can be soldered from the back of the card.\nWith the Pico on headers or in a socket the port is unusable: use a micro-USB OTG adapter\non the Pico (with jumper J7) instead, as on v1.3.0. Never use both at the same time.\nVBUS from ISA +5V via F1 (resettable, 0.5 A hold). The Pico VBUS pin is not used for this port.\nJ11 takes a USB-A OR a USB-C receptacle. R25/R26 (Rp 56k = default USB power) tell a USB-C\ndevice that this is a 5 V source; with a USB-A socket they are not connected (fit them anyway).\nU12 (ESD array, SOT-23-6) is optional."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
